<p>I agree with Pair of Ducks. There is nothing here other than something imagined that makes it an SCP. It's just an animal. The fact that a miniature, somehow mammalian, pterodactyl exists is not a threat to the public in any way, and the suggestion that more might live in South America makes it strictly an animal with no strange qualities other than looking like a pterodactyl. It wouldn't just be "mysterious." Biologists would study it. Keeping it from the scientific world would just be silly. Weird animals pop up all the time. No one tries to hide them.</p>

