			<div class="content" id="post-content-1240473">
									

<p>I have some suggestions to make this cute SCP a little stranger.<br />
One idea is that anomalous traits don't appear unless more of the pterodactyls (maybe a weird flock effect). An addendum could be included on the discovery of more of the species, which may hint on why 346 needs to be contained.<br />
The article mentions that 346 comes from an isolated species, but perhaps the females of the species have some kind of scary sexual-dimorphism that make the females larger and more dangerous than the males.<br />
Or maybe you don't want to go the dangerous route. Not everything needs to be scary and harmful.<br />
But if you like the dangerous sexual-dimorphism, I have an idea to make the females a bit more supernatural: make them Thunderbirds. The females would be predators that shoot lightning and the males harmless breeders and nest-tenders.<br />
I know that we already have some electric animals (<a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-594">SCP-594</a>), but I think this one could easily be adapted to become a unique member of that club.</p>

